  "description": "<p>In case sensitive operating systems, attempting to create an external binary from a local file uri will fail if there are any capital letters in the file path. For example:</p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\ncurl -XPUT -H<span class=\"code-quote\">\"Link: &lt;file:<span class=\"code-comment\">///path/to/CAPS/TEST.txt&gt;; rel=\\\"</span>http://fedora.info/definitions/fcrepo#ExternalContent\\<span class=\"code-quote\">\"; handling=\\\"</span>proxy\\<span class=\"code-quote\">\"; type=\\\"</span>text/plain\\\"\" http://localhost:8080/fcrepo/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/case_sensitive</span>\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>Will return:</p>\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>Path did not match any allowed external content paths: file:///path/to/CAPS/TEST.txt</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>Even though the file exists and is within a path allowed by the fcrepo.external.content.allowed config file</p>",
